# Copy to .env, fill in the values, then load it before running a command:
#   cd demo/operator && cp .env.example .env && set -a && source .env && set +a
#   npm run operator      # the demo's operator service
#   npm run deploy        # one-time: deploy the demo contracts on two registered domains

# =====================================================================
# npm run operator  (long-running: the demo's operator service, from demo/operator)
# =====================================================================
#
# Runs everything the demo's operators are responsible for in one process: the relayer for
# both domains (as above), Bank A's back office (reserve pool liquidity for approved payment
# orders and execute the payment), the onboarding faucet (gas drip, demo EUR mint, registry
# entries at both banks) and the HTTP API the frontend uses (/api/config, /api/status,
# /api/onboard). Addresses come from deployments/<DEPLOYMENT>.json (see npm run deploy).

# --- Required ---

# L1_RPC_URL=                       # shared with the blocks above
# DEPLOYMENT=testnet                # deployments/<name>.json, or a path to a JSON file
# OPERATOR_KEY=                     # the demo's admin key; default for every other key below

# --- Optional ---

# VALIDATOR_KEYS=0x..,0x..          # registered validators (default: OPERATOR_KEY)
# SUBMITTER_KEY=                    # pays submitStateSignature / relayDomainMessage
# BANK_KEY=                         # BANK on both L2Banks and the pool locker
# FAUCET_KEY=                       # funds drips and mints demo EUR
# DOMAIN_A_RPC_URL=                 # default $L1_RPC_URL/domain/<A chain id>
# DOMAIN_B_RPC_URL=
# PORT=8787
# CORS_ORIGIN=*                     # the frontend proxies /api, so * is fine
# FAUCET_DRIP_WEI=500000000000000000          # 0.5 MON per onboarding
# FAUCET_DRIP_BELOW_WEI=300000000000000000    # only drip below this balance
# FAUCET_MINT_EUR_WEI=1000000000000000000000  # 1000 demo EUR per onboarding
# FAUCET_RECEIVE_LIMIT_WEI=100000000000000000000000  # registry limit (100000)
# FAUCET_COOLDOWN_MS=600000         # per address
# FAUCET_PER_IP_LIMIT=10            # per cooldown window
# LOCK_TTL_SECONDS=600
# POLL_INTERVAL_MS=500              # delay between passes (relayer, bank agent, queued jobs)
# ATTEST_INTERVAL_MS=60000
# RPC_GATEWAY=true                  # serve /rpc and /rpc/domain/<id> (what the frontend uses)

# --- Node access through an ssh port-forward (instead of L1_RPC_URL) ---
# For a node whose domain routes are not published: the service runs `ssh -N -L` to the
# node's localhost RPC and talks to the forward. Use a key the node restricts to forwarding:
#   restrict,port-forwarding,permitopen="127.0.0.1:8080",command="/bin/false" ssh-ed25519 ...
# RPC_SSH_HOST=swe-013.devcore4.com
# RPC_SSH_PORT=9022
# RPC_SSH_USER=monad
# RPC_SSH_KEY=                      # private key contents (multi-line), or RPC_SSH_KEY_FILE=path
# RPC_SSH_KNOWN_HOSTS=              # "swe-013.devcore4.com ssh-ed25519 AAAA..." to pin the host key
# RPC_SSH_REMOTE=127.0.0.1:8080
# RPC_SSH_LOCAL_PORT=18080

# =====================================================================
# npm run deploy  (one-time: layer the bank demo on two registered domains, from demo/operator)
# =====================================================================
#
# L1_RPC_URL=... ADMIN_KEY=0x... [BANK_KEY=0x...] [DEPLOYMENT=testnet] [POOL_USD_LIQUIDITY=1000000]
# Reads hub / spokes / viewing keys / start blocks from deployments/<DEPLOYMENT>.json and
# writes the demo addresses back into it. Run `forge build` first.
